# What this repository carries is the host: the code that serves a drive, the
# templates and starters it seeds one from, the tests, and the tools that keep
# it honest. What it does not carry is anybody's drive, anybody's machine, or
# anything a session leaves behind. If a change is to your documents, it is
# already saved — that is what the drive is for — and there is nothing to
# commit.

# ---- dependencies and secrets ----------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.env
.env.local
# API keys the Agents settings panel writes. Never under the drive — backups
# copy the drive, and `.marble/` is conversation data. The glob covers the
# atomic-write temp files (`.agent-keys.local.<pid>.<hex>.tmp`) too.
.agent-keys.local*

# ---- the drive: the owner's, not the repository's --------------------------
# The default drive root. A drive belongs to whoever is running the host, not
# to this repository — and `.marble/` under it is their history.
drive/
# Hand-made copies of documents, kept beside the drive rather than in it.
backups/
# The daily-document skill's memory of its one reader: what it has shown, the
# to-dos he typed, where he lives. The skill is code and stays; its memory is
# his, and it changes on every morning's run.
.claude/skills/my-day/state/

# ---- this machine ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.log
*.pid
__pycache__/
# Claude Code's per-machine settings and the worktrees it checks out. A
# worktree is a checkout of this repository, so committing the path stores a
# gitlink to a branch that lives only on one laptop.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
# Hook config that names absolute paths on one laptop.
.codex/
# Local design-hook detector config (per machine)
.impeccable/

# ---- what a session leaves behind ------------------------------------------
# Screenshots, one-off patches, generated pages. A script worth keeping moves
# to `tools/`; the rest is never read back after the run that made it.
scratchpad/
*.heapsnapshot
# Brainstorm servers, their ports, tokens and pids.
.superpowers/
